WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.860
In Galilee, tax collectors gathered
money for Herod or for Rome.

2
00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:06.610
Many took extra.

3
00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:08.830
Their neighbours saw
them as collaborators,

4
00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:10.470
and as sinners.

5
00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:13.970
Respectable religious people
kept well away from them.

6
00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:19.010
Yet one day, Jesus walks past a tax office
by the lake and says to the man sitting

7
00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:21.110
there: Follow me.

8
00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:25.970
So why did Jesus keep choosing the
company that respectable people avoided?

9
00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:30.720
In this mission, you'll meet Levi, the
tax collector who got up and followed,

10
00:00:30.770 --> 00:00:32.780
and the people who objected.

11
00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:36.820
Then you'll see what his choices
mean for Christians today.

12
00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:41.940
Your mission: find out why Jesus kept
choosing the company that respectable people

13
00:00:41.990 --> 00:00:42.760
avoided.
